.\" Process this file with
.\" groff -man -Tascii elfobj.3
.TH ELFOBJ 3 "February 2026" "Substrate" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
elfobj, elf_open, elf_open_memory, elf_write_file, elf_close, elf_add_section, elf_section_set_data, elf_find_section, elf_add_symbol, elf_find_symbol, elf_add_relocation, elf_link, elf_validate, elf_hash_sysv, elf_hash_gnu \- ELF object handling API
.SH LIBRARY
ELF object library (libelfobj, -lelfobj)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <elfobj.h>
.PP
.BI "elf_err_t elf_open(const char *path, elfobj_t **out);"
.br
.BI "elf_err_t elf_open_memory(const void *buf, size_t size, elfobj_t **out);"
.br
.BI "elf_err_t elf_write_file(elfobj_t *obj, const char *path);"
.br
.BI "void elf_close(elfobj_t *obj);"
.PP
.BI "elf_section_t *elf_add_section(elfobj_t *obj, const char *name, uint32_t type, uint64_t flags);"
.br
.BI "elf_err_t elf_section_set_data(elf_section_t *section, const void *data, size_t size);"
.br
.BI "elf_section_t *elf_find_section(elfobj_t *obj, const char *name);"
.PP
.BI "elf_symbol_t *elf_add_symbol(elfobj_t *obj, const char *name, uint64_t value,"
.br
.BI "    uint64_t size, uint8_t bind, uint8_t type);"
.br
.BI "elf_symbol_t *elf_find_symbol(elfobj_t *obj, const char *name);"
.PP
.BI "elf_err_t elf_add_relocation(elf_section_t *section, uint64_t offset, elf_symbol_t *symbol,"
.br
.BI "    uint32_t type, int64_t addend);"
.PP
.BI "elf_err_t elf_link(elfobj_t **inputs, size_t count, elfobj_t **output);"
.br
.BI "elf_err_t elf_validate(elfobj_t *obj, char **diagnostics);"
.PP
.BI "uint32_t elf_hash_sysv(const char *name);"
.br
.BI "uint32_t elf_hash_gnu(const char *name);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B libelfobj
library provides structured reading, mutation, validation, and writing of ELF objects.
It supports ET_REL, ET_EXEC, ET_DYN, and read-only ET_CORE parsing.
.PP
Objects loaded via
.B elf_open
or
.B elf_open_memory
are parsed with bounds checking. Creation and mutation flows use
.B elf_create
plus section/symbol/relocation APIs, and the result is serialized with
.BR elf_write_file .
.PP
.B elf_validate
returns an allocated diagnostics string describing malformed offsets,
overlap conditions, and relocation/symbol consistency issues.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Functions returning
.B elf_err_t
use
.B ELF_OK
on success. Pointer-returning APIs return NULL on failure.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_IO
Input/output failure while reading or writing files.
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_FORMAT
Malformed ELF structure, unsupported table layout, or invalid metadata.
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_RELOC
Relocation semantic failure (unsupported backend/type/application).
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_OOM
Memory allocation failure.
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_BOUNDS
Offset/size pair exceeds input bounds.
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_UNSUPPORTED
Feature is valid ELF but not implemented by current backend/path.
.TP
.B ELF_ERR_STATE
Invalid API call ordering or NULL/invalid object state.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a minimal relocatable object with one text section and one symbol:
.PP
.nf
elfobj_t *obj = elf_create(ET_REL, EM_386, ELFOBJ_CLASS_32, ELFOBJ_ENDIAN_LE);
elf_section_t *text = elf_add_section(obj, ".text", SHT_PROGBITS, SHF_ALLOC|SHF_EXECINSTR);
unsigned char code[] = { 0x90, 0xC3 };
elf_section_set_data(text, code, sizeof(code));
elf_add_symbol(obj, "func", 0, sizeof(code), STB_GLOBAL, STT_FUNC);
elf_write_file(obj, "out.o");
elf_close(obj);
.fi
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Distinct
.B elfobj_t
instances may be processed concurrently. Mutable operations are not internally synchronized.
.SH SEE ALSO
ld(1), objdump(1), readelf(1), elf(5)
